# FLOOR 3 — AREA GENERATION TABLES
*Roll before the session. Each area requires three rolls: Environment, Obstacle, and Guard Composition.*
*Results combine to create the full area on the fly.*

---

## HOW TO USE

For each area, roll:
- **1d6** → Environment Variant (changes the visual and flavor of the area)
- **1d6** → Obstacle Variant (determines what the players are up against mechanically)
- **1d8** → Guard Composition (determines who and how many guards are present)

The Check Options are listed under each Obstacle result. The Obelisk hint updates to match whatever was rolled. (Use a 3d6 for environment and its respective obstacle and a d8 for the guards that patrol the area)

Guards are individually weak but highly intelligent and will always pick the best options for them

Entering an area roll a d20 on a 10 and below, Players must make a Strength-based or Dex-based or Wis-based Stealth check when entering an area 

When players make a check and fails they may risk guards appearing.

---

## MASTER GUARD COMPOSITION TABLE
*Roll 1d8. Used for all six areas unless an area specifies its own table.*

| d8 | Composition | Total Guards | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 6 Scouts | 6 | Light presence. Patrol only. |
| 2 | 2 Sentinel + 4 Scouts | 6 | Standard gate/entry setup. |
| 3 | 4 Sentinels + 2 Scout | 6 | Holding pattern. Melee-heavy. |
| 4 | 4 Scouts + 4 Sentinels | 8 | Balanced patrol and hold. |
| 5 | 6 Scouts + 4 Sentinel | 10 | Ranged-heavy. Perimeter sweep. |
| 6 | 4 Scouts + 4 Sentinels + 1 Wardens | 9 | Standard heavy response. |
| 7 | 6 Scouts + 4 Sentinels + 1 Wardens | 11 | Active patrol with anchor. |
| 8 | 8 Scouts + 4 Sentinels + 2 Wardens | 14 | Full alert deployment. Treat as if area is already at Alert Level 1. |

**DM Note:** Roll at the start of the session before players enter the floor. If a Patrol Surge trap triggers (minute 60), add 1 Scout to whatever composition was rolled, per area.

