# AREA 2 — THE LUNAR BARRACKS COURT
*Northeast path*

---

## Environment — Roll 1d6

| d6 | What the Area Looks Like |
|---|---|
| 1 | **Open Parade Ground** — Wide flat courtyard, almost no cover. Three stone pillars in a line are the only interruptions. The far door is clearly visible from the entrance. |
| 2 | **Training Yard with Equipment** — Obstacles and wooden training posts scattered around the yard. Provides cover but also increases the number of surfaces that generate noise when brushed against. |
| 3 | **Tiered Terrace Court** — The courtyard drops in levels, with three steps between each tier. Guards patrol different tiers; sight lines between levels are interrupted. |
| 4 | **Night Garden** — The court is partially overgrown with moonflowers and silver hedges, waist-high, that create natural lanes. Guards follow the lanes too. |
| 5 | **Paved Market Space** — Rows of locked supply crates and equipment racks divide the courtyard into corridors. The guards navigate them at predictable angles. |
| 6 | **Flooded Courtyard** — 2 inches of standing water across the full court. Movement is quieter than expected, but footprints are visible. Any running causes splashing that automatically alerts nearby guards. |

---

## Obstacle — Roll 1d6

| d6 | Obstacle Type | Primary Check Options | Obelisk Hint |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Multiple Crossing Guards** | WIS (Perception) DC 12 — map patrol timing before crossing. DEX (Stealth) DC 14 — cross during the gap. Failure on Stealth without prior Perception check triggers immediate pursuit. | *Several guards, multiple routes. Patience first. Movement second.* |
| 2 | **Single Long Patrol Route** | DEX (Stealth) DC 13 — shadow the guard's movement along the longer arc. WIS (Insight) DC 11 — read the guard's pace to predict when they will stop or turn. | *One guard covering a wide area. If you can read their rhythm, you have the whole courtyard.* |
| 3 | **Locked Far Door** | DEX (Sleight of Hand) DC 14 — pick the door at the far end (while avoiding guards). INT (Investigation) DC 12 — find a guard carrying the key (requires identifying which guard, then pickpocketing or neutralizing). DEX (Sleight of Hand or Stealth) second check required. | *The door at the far side is locked. Someone on this side has the key.* |
| 4 | **Guard Conversation Block** | CHA (Deception) DC 13 — interrupt a guard pair in conversation with a plausible reason to be there. CHA (Persuasion) DC 15 — convince them to clear the route entirely. DEX (Stealth) DC 15 — slip past while they are talking (harder; they are facing the route). | *Two guards have stopped to talk directly in the path. This is either a social problem or a very careful stealth problem.* |
| 5 | **Open Ground Sprint** | DEX (Athletics or Acrobatics) DC 14 — cross the open space in the window between patrols. Must succeed WIS (Perception) DC 11 first to identify the window, or the sprint DC becomes 17. | *No cover, but there is a timing window. The whole problem is reading when to move and being fast enough.* |
| 6 | **Noise Hazard Terrain** | DEX (Acrobatics) DC 13 — navigate the hazardous surface without generating noise (water, crates, training equipment — matched to Environment roll). Failure triggers immediate attention from nearest guard. | *The ground itself is the problem. Movement here is loud if you aren't careful.* |

---

## Guard Composition — Use Master Table (1d8)
**Area 2 Modifier:** Add +1 Scout to any result. This is a barracks — it is always busier than other areas.

**Area 2 Special Rule — Noise Propagation:** Any combat or failed check in Area 2 affects Area 3 and the center courtyard simultaneously. Guards in those areas raise to Alert Level 1 for 15 minutes.

---

## What's Always Inside
A supply room. Contains:
- **1 lootable item** (roll from loot table)
- **Guard Schedule Board** — same benefit as Patrol Log (they do not stack)

