# AREA 3 — THE MOON SAGE'S LIBRARY
*East path*

---

## Environment — Roll 1d6

| d6 | What the Area Looks Like |
|---|---|
| 1 | **Single Heavy Door** — Carved stone door, sealed, with glowing inscription across the lintel. No windows at ground level. A warden stands directly in front of it. |
| 2 | **Open Colonnade Entry** — The library has no wall, only a row of columns. Silk screens hang between them. The inside is visible but the entry is clearly guarded by both a stationed guard and a rooftop scout. |
| 3 | **Locked Reading Pavilion** — A separate smaller building in front of the main library. Its door is unlocked; the inner passage to the real library is gated. The first room is unguarded; the gate inside has a guard beyond it. |
| 4 | **Overgrown Archive** — Silver vines have grown across the lower windows and most of the entry arch. The building looks half-abandoned but the guards are very present. The vines can be climbed to reach a high open window. |
| 5 | **Underground Entrance** — The library is built into a slope. The visible entrance is the upper floor; a lower entrance exists via stone stairs cut into the hillside, partly obscured by decorative stonework. |
| 6 | **Two-Door Security** — Two sequential doors, each requiring separate handling. The outer door is social/knowledge-based. The inner door is physical. Only one guard per door. |

---

## Obstacle — Roll 1d6

| d6 | Obstacle Type | Primary Check Options | Obelisk Hint |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Inscription Code Phrase** | INT (Arcana) DC 14 — read the inscription and speak the correct response. INT (History) DC 13 — recognize the ceremonial format and guess the response structure. WIS (Perception) DC 11 — notice a worn etching near the base with a partial translation. | *Glowing inscriptions on the lintel. This building wants a correct response, not force.* |
| 2 | **Secondary Entrance** | INT (History) DC 13 — recall that Lunarian buildings of this type always include a maintenance entry. WIS (Perception) DC 12 — spot the secondary entry from the exterior. DEX (Stealth) DC 11 — enter through it unobserved (lower DC because this route avoids the guards entirely). | *Something about the building's layout from above suggests it wasn't designed to have only one way in.* |
| 3 | **Ceremonial Gesture Sequence** | WIS (Religion) DC 15 — identify the correct lunar deity crest and perform the associated gesture. CHA (Performance) DC 13 — perform a plausible ceremonial greeting convincingly enough that the guard allows entry. INT (Arcana) DC 12 first — identify what ceremony this is (grants advantage on Religion or Performance if successful). | *This entrance is ceremonial. Conduct matters as much as knowledge here.* |
| 4 | **Warden Persuasion** | CHA (Persuasion) DC 14 — convince the Warden you have authorized access. CHA (Deception) DC 13 — present false credentials. WIS (Insight) DC 11 first — read what kind of authority the Warden responds to (grants advantage on whichever social skill is chosen). | *The Warden is the obstacle. This is a conversation.* |
| 5 | **Roof Access** | STR (Athletics) DC 13 — climb the colonnade or overgrowth to reach the high window. DEX (Acrobatics) DC 12 — navigate the rooftop entry without making noise. Scout on rooftop must be avoided or neutralized first. | *There is a high opening visible from above. Getting to it requires going up, not through.* |
| 6 | **Distraction and Entry** | CHA (Deception) DC 12 — create a plausible distraction elsewhere that draws the stationed guard off position for 3 minutes. DEX (Stealth) DC 12 — enter during the window. Both checks required in sequence. Failure on the second check occurs with the first guard away — only one guard responds. | *The guard needs to be somewhere else for a moment. Manufacture that moment.* |

---

## Guard Composition — Use Master Table (1d8)
**Area 3 Special Rule:** Regardless of the composition rolled, one guard is always **a Warden** stationed at the primary entrance. Wardens here have been specifically briefed — they are harder to deceive (add +2 to social DCs against them) but respond appropriately to correct ceremonial conduct.

---

## What's Always Inside
Two lootable items (this area is richer). Contains:
- **2 lootable items** (roll twice from loot table; one may be a Spell Card)
- **Lunar Atlas** — advantage on the Obelisk Crescent Alcove Perception check

