# AREA 4 — THE Sun-Drenched Bastion
*Southeast path*

---

## Environment — Roll 1d6

| d6 | What the Area Looks Like |
|---|---|
| 1 | **Three Open Terraces** — Wide stone steps between three levels, minimal cover. Guards are visible between levels. The target is at the top. |
| 2 | **Moonflower Hedge Maze** — Dense silver-leafed hedges divide the terrace into corridors. Guards follow the corridors too. Sight lines are short in all directions. |
| 3 | **Statue Garden Terraces** — Large stone statues of Lunarian figures on each level, tall enough to stand behind. Predictable cover, predictable patrol routes that wind between them. |
| 4 | **Flooded Lower Level** — The first terrace is knee-deep in reflecting water from an overflowing basin. The second and third levels are dry. Stealth in the lower level is impossible at normal movement. |
| 5 | **Collapsed Upper Terrace** — The top level has partially fallen. The stone plinth with the target is still intact on a stable section, but reaching it requires navigating collapsed sections. No guards on the top level — they patrol the second level only. |
| 6 | **Formal Garden with Benches** — Open stone paths between trimmed silver shrubs and benches. Three rest spots the guards use during their routes, which creates very predictable stop points. |

---

## Obstacle — Roll 1d6

| d6 | Obstacle Type | Primary Check Options | Obelisk Hint |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Guard Timing — Two Routes** | WIS (Perception) DC 13 — time both patrol loops to find the crossing window. DEX (Stealth) DC 13 — move between levels during the window. Failure on Perception means the window is misjudged — check again at +3 DC. | *Two guards, different loops, different timing. From above the pattern is clear. From ground level, less so.* |
| 2 | **Scent-Based Detection** | WIS (Nature) DC 12 — identify the moonflowers and know that crushing them disrupts Lunarian senses. 1 minute to gather and apply. Grants advantage on Stealth for the rest of this area attempt. DEX (Stealth) DC 15 if not applied. | *The plants here have properties. The guards' senses aren't purely sight.* |
| 3 | **Pressure Plate Field** | WIS (Perception) DC 14 — spot the plates before stepping on them. DEX (Acrobatics) DC 13 — navigate through the field. Failure on Perception means a random plate triggers — alert raised by 1 and guards rush toward the level. | *The ground on at least one level is uneven in a suspicious way. Look before stepping.* |
| 4 | **Locked Final Grate** | DEX (Sleight of Hand) DC 14 — pick the iron grate at the top. STR (Athletics) DC 16 — force it (noisy; +1 alert). INT (Investigation) DC 13 — find that one of the guards is carrying a spare key. | *There's a locked grate at the top. The obstacle isn't just getting there — it's getting in when you arrive.* |
| 5 | **Guard Call and Response** | Guards on this terrace use a verbal call-and-response check at irregular intervals. INT (History) DC 13 or INT (Arcana) DC 12 — identify the correct response from context. CHA (Deception) DC 14 — fake the response if caught mid-route. | *The guards here communicate with each other at intervals. Being caught between call points without knowing the response is a problem.* |
| 6 | **Narrow Ledge Route** | DEX (Acrobatics) DC 13 — traverse the outer ledge of the terrace wall to bypass the guarded path entirely. STR (Athletics) DC 11 for anyone in medium or heavy armor (movement is restricted). This route has no guards — but a fall is a 10ft drop. | *The wall has a ledge on the outside face. Not the intended route. Possibly the better one.* |

---

## Guard Composition — Use Master Table (1d8)
**Area 4 Modifier:** Subtract 1 Scout from any result (minimum 0 Scouts). Sentinels and Wardens remain as rolled. This area uses fewer fast-moving scouts and more positioned guards due to the terrace layout.

**Area 4 Special Rule — Patrol Log Benefit:** If the party has the Patrol Log from Area 1 or the Guard Schedule from Area 2, all Perception checks to read patrol timing in this area are made with advantage.

---

## What's Always Inside
The stone plinth at the top. Contains:
- **1 lootable item** (roll from loot table)
- **Hand-Drawn Partial Map** — shows estate layout including a label on the gap between Areas 3 and 6 reading *"sealed? check later."*

