# AREA 6 — THE PRAYER HALL
*West path*

---

## Environment — Roll 1d6

| d6 | What the Area Looks Like |
|---|---|
| 1 | **Open Pavilion with Silk Screens** — Wide pavilion, open sides, silk screens filtering the cold blue light. The ceremony is visible from outside. The attendant is easily approachable. |
| 2 | **Walled Garden Shrine** — Low stone walls surround a garden with a central altar. One entrance gate (unlocked). The ceremony is happening at the altar in the garden's center. |
| 3 | **Elevated Platform Hall** — The prayer hall sits on a raised stone platform, reached by a short staircase. The elevation means the attendant can see anyone approaching from a distance. |
| 4 | **Interior Shrine Room** — A fully enclosed room with a single door. The ceremony is happening inside; the door is ajar. A scout is posted outside with a clear view of the approach path. |
| 5 | **Double-Hall Design** — Two connected chambers. The outer chamber is empty and unguarded; the inner chamber has the attendant, the altar, and the guards. The transition between rooms is the key chokepoint. |
| 6 | **Courtyard Ceremony** — The ritual is being conducted in the open, in a small secondary courtyard adjacent to the prayer hall itself. Multiple guards form a ceremonial ring around the attendant, facing outward. |

---

## Obstacle — Roll 1d6

| d6 | Obstacle Type | Primary Check Options | Obelisk Hint |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Ceremonial Approach** | CHA (Persuasion) DC 14 — approach with appropriate conduct and request passage. CHA (Performance) DC 13 — participate in the ceremony convincingly enough to be granted access. WIS (Insight) DC 11 first — read the attendant's disposition (grants advantage on either social check). | *The ceremony is in progress. This is a social space. How you approach matters as much as what you say.* |
| 2 | **Disguise and Blend** | CHA (Deception) DC 13 — pass as a Lunarian attendant (requires either Lunarian robes found elsewhere, or a convincing physical disguise). DEX (Stealth) DC 14 — approach without disguise while the attendant is absorbed in the ritual. | *The people here look a particular way and behave a particular way. Matching that is the path.* |
| 3 | **The Guard Ring** | WIS (Perception) DC 12 — identify a gap in the ceremonial guard ring. DEX (Stealth) DC 14 — slip through the gap when the ceremony reaches its loud climactic moment (the sound masks movement). | *The guards here form a pattern. There are gaps if you can read them and time your movement to when the ceremony covers the noise.* |
| 4 | **Attendant Conversation** | CHA (Persuasion) DC 13 — engage the attendant in direct conversation and navigate naturally toward the passage request. WIS (Insight) DC 11 — identify the topic the attendant most wants to discuss (reduces Persuasion DC to 10 if used first). CHA (Deception) DC 15 — lie convincingly about having official business beyond the hall. | *One person stands between you and the passage. Talking to them is not dangerous. Getting what you want from the conversation is the skill.* |
| 5 | **Noise-Sensitive Hall** | DEX (Stealth) DC 15 — move through the hall in complete silence (this area amplifies sound; the DC is higher than elsewhere). INT (Investigation) DC 12 — identify the silent path through the hall by examining the floor for loose stones or resonant surfaces before moving. | *This space was built for silence. It enforces that. You will need to be more careful here than anywhere else on the floor.* |
| 6 | **Ritual Participation** | INT (Religion) DC 13 — know enough about the Lunarian ceremony to participate appropriately. CHA (Performance) DC 14 — participate convincingly without the knowledge base. WIS (Religion or Insight) DC 11 — watch long enough to mimic the gestures before participating (reduces either DC by 2). | *The ceremony is ongoing. Joining it correctly is not an insult — it is access.* |

---

## Guard Composition — Special Table for Area 6 — Roll 1d6

*Area 6 uses a different composition table. It is a ceremonial location — guards here are positioned, not mobile.*

| d6 | Composition | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | 1 Scout (entrance) + 1 Warden (altar, stationary) | Minimum ceremonial presence. |
| 2 | 2 Scouts (entrance and perimeter) + 1 Warden (altar) | Standard presence. |
| 3 | 1 Scout + 2 Sentinels (flanking the attendant) + 1 Warden | Full honor guard. Sentinels face outward. |
| 4 | 3 Scouts (perimeter ring) + 1 Warden | Perimeter-heavy. The interior is actually less guarded. |
| 5 | 2 Sentinels + 2 Wardens | No scouts. Two heavy guards, both positioned at the altar, both watching the entrance. |
| 6 | 4 Scouts (ceremonial ring, facing outward) + 1 Sentinel + 1 Warden | Maximum ceremonial guard. Stealth DCs in this area increase by 3 due to the full perimeter ring. |

**Area 6 Special Rule — Sound Propagation:** Any combat in Area 6 is the worst outcome on the floor. Area 3, Area 5, and the center courtyard all receive Alert Level 1 simultaneously. This is the loudest area if it goes wrong.

**Area 6 Special Rule — The Clue:** If the party successfully engages the attendant in conversation (any social check succeeds), the attendant mentions the old crescent passage between Areas 3 and 6 in the course of natural conversation. They do not think it is significant. It is the most direct verbal clue to the Crescent Alcove.

